    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125">

                <pb facs="0105" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/1178: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-12-15T00:00:00-03:00">December 15,
                            1939—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received December 16—12:41a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>434. Department’s circular December 15, 1 p.m. Aranha approves “as far as it
                    goes” but feels strongly that this should be only a preliminary step toward
                    stronger action as set out in his first suggestion of my 432, December 15, 2
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>He talked on the telephone this afternoon with Cantilo<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d125-f1"/> who is in general agreement with his attitude.</p>
                <p>Aranha says he expects arrival here tomorrow of English <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Renown</hi> and an aircraft carrier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d125-f1" n="19" xml:id="d125-f1-content">
                <p>José M. Cantilo, Argentine Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
